Brief explanation:
This code finds the integer square root of a non‑negative number x using binary search.
It searches between 1 and x/2, compares mid * mid with x, and narrows the range until the largest integer whose square is ≤ x is found. Using long prevents overflow during multiplication.
Complexities:

Time Complexity: O(log x) — binary search halves the range each step
Space Complexity: O(1) — uses constant extra space
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

class Solution {
    public int mySqrt(int x) {
        if(x<2) return x;
        int l=1;
        int r=x/2;
        while(l<=r){
            int mid=l+(r-l)/2;
            long square= (long)mid*mid;
            if(square==x){
                return mid;
            }else if(square<x){
                l=mid+1;
            }else{
                r=mid-1;
            }
        }
        return r;
        
    }
}
